% Dominique Makowski - publications.
%
% Ground truth for publications, and a sibling of PROFILE.md rather than a file
% inside cv/: other projects (lab website, biosketches, funder portals) draw
% from this repo, and they should not have to reach into the CV's build folder
% to do it. See PROFILE.md > Publications.
%
% This file holds FACTS ONLY - who wrote what, where it appeared, and how to
% find it. Which theme an entry belongs to, whether the CV shows it, and in what
% order are editorial decisions, and they live in cv/content/publications.yml
% against these cite keys. The same split as PROFILE.md -> cv/content/*.yml, one
% level down.
%
% Conventions:
%
%   - Cite keys are <firstauthor><year><word>, matching the convention already
%     used by the publication URLs on dominiquemakowski.github.io. Entries with
%     no year yet (preprints under review) use <firstauthor>_<word>.
%   - UTF-8 throughout, not TeX escapes. Nothing here is compiled by LaTeX; the
%     CV reads it with cv/tools/build_publications.py.
%   - `doi` is preferred over `url`. Give `url` only when there is no DOI, or
%     when the linked copy is the one worth reading (an author PDF).
%   - `status = {under review}` for work not yet accepted. Such entries carry no
%     `year`, which is what sorts them to the top of their theme.
%   - `equal = {1,2}` marks shared authorship by author position, and
%     `equalnote` says what kind. The renderer turns those positions into
%     asterisks.
%   - Media coverage, podcasts and public talks are NOT publications and are not
%     here; they are PROFILE.md > Media and Public Engagement.

